    "name": "list_binary_search",
    "doc": "list_binary_search(xs, x) = Some(i) with xs[i] == x when x occurs in the sorted list xs, or None when it does not. With duplicate targets any valid index satisfies the contract — the specific index is spec-silent. Hand body at the executed standard (the G5 scope-around, STDLIB_SCOPE.md 2.6): the body is a scan, because generated Rust cannot index a Vec by an Int variable (the language has no usize — G5), so the While-form binary search cannot compile; the frozen contract is the search semantics above, and per-entry complexity is deliberately outside the gate (STDLIB_SCOPE.md 3). Tier-2: executed-exact on the full battery; at 1.3 its element rows encode, but its require: is not assumable in the crown route — list_is_sorted's contract is quantifier-shaped, with no expression-level denotation for the precondition machinery — so no Verified claim is made (LIST_ENCODER_SCOPE.md 3.3; Phase 144 measurement).",
